\begin{center}
    {\Large\sffamily\bfseries\color{brandnavy} Pedagogical Architecture \& How to Use This Book}
\end{center}
\vspace{1cm}
\noindent
This textbook is structured around the six rigorous units of the CSR101 curriculum:
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=1.8em, itemsep=6pt]
    \item \textbf{Formal Mathematical \& Architectural Definitions:} Every concept begins with formal language semantics, CPython internals, or asymptotic complexity models.
    \item \textbf{Syntax Specification \& Code Invariants:} High-yield code examples illustrate idiomatic Python 3.11+ standards following PEP 8.
    \item \textbf{Step-by-Step Worked Problems:} Practical algorithms with explicit execution traces, time complexity derivations, and memory layout diagrams.
    \item \textbf{Examiner Traps \& Edge Cases:} Callout warnings highlighting standard examination traps, tricky operator precedence nuances, and silent runtime bugs.
\end{enumerate}
